wered by USB2ANY_3.3V\\". I will assume a separate net for ISO GND is not explicitly defined in SCUD nets list, but standard practice implies it. However, I will stick to SCUD nets. If no ISO_GND is listed, I might have to leave it or use GND if the SCUD implies common ground (which defeats isolation). SCUD says \\"GND is tied to CELL0...\\". Let\'s look at J17. J17 has GND? J17-1 is likely GND. I will create a net ISO_GND for safety if not in SCUD, but SCUD is authoritative. SCUD says \\"J3 Pin 1: GND\\". J17 pinout not fully detailed for GND. I will assume Side 1 uses a net named \\"ISO_GND\\" implicitly or just leave it unconnected if not specified. Wait, SCUD says \\"GND is tied to CELL0... establishing the reference potential for the low-voltage side.\\" This implies the BMS side is the \\"low voltage side\\" relative to the stack? No, BMS is High Voltage. MCU is Low Voltage.\\n      Actually, let\'s look at U2 connections again.\\n      Side 1 (MCU): USB2ANY_3.3V.\\n      Side 2 (BMS): CVDD_CO.\\n      I will connect Side 2 GND to net.GND (BMS Ground).\\n      Side 1 GND needs a net. I\'ll call it \\"GND_ISO\\".\\n      */}\\n      <net name=\\"GND_ISO\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".U2 > .GND1\\" to=\\"net.GND_ISO\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".U2 > .GND2\\" to=\\"net.GND\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".U2 > .VCC2\\" to=\\"net.CVDD_CO\\" />\\n      \\n      <trace from=\\".C57 > .pin1\\" to=\\"net.USB2ANY_3.3V\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".C57 > .pin2\\" to=\\"net.GND_ISO\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".C58 > .pin1\\" to=\\"net.CVDD_CO\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".C58 > .pin2\\" to=\\"net.GND\\" />\\n\\n      <trace from=\\".J18 > .pin1\\" to=\\"net.CVDD\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".J18 > .pin2\\" to=\\"net.CVDD_CO\\" />\\n\\n      {/* U2 Signals */}\\n      {/* TX Path: MCU -> BMS */}\\n      <trace from=\\".J17 > .pin7\\" to=\\"net.USB2ANY_TX_3.3\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".U2 > .INB\\" to=\\"net.USB2ANY_TX_3.3\\" />\\n      <trace from=\\".U2 > .OUTB\\" to=\\